    ],
    "text": "Secretaries of the 1st and 4th Petitioners.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.507699966430664,
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      425.27,
      537.82,
      436.56
    ],
    "text": "The Petitioners claim that formulating regulations to give effect to the provisions of the",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      93.73,
      443.59,
      537.81,
      457.26
    ],
    "text": "Industrial Disputes Act No. 43 of 1950 (as amended) (IDA Act) is exclusively vested in the 2nd",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.507699966430664,
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      466.61,
      537.82,
      477.9
    ],
    "text": "Respondent Minister and must be exercised in terms of section 39(1) of the IDA Act, all such",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      93.73,
      487.25,
      537.81,
      498.54
    ],
    "text": "regulations tabled in Parliament, approved and notification of such approval gazetted in order",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      507.95,
      474.27,
      519.24
    ],
    "text": "for them to have legal validity and effect as set out in section 39(2) of the IDA Act.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      526.33,
      537.81,
      539.94
    ],
    "text": "They further claim that it is clear from the terms of section 39(2) of the IDA Act that the 2nd",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.507699966430664,
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      549.29,
      537.81,
      560.58
    ],
    "text": "Respondent Minister is the sole authority empowered in law to formulate such regulations inter",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      569.99,
      537.81,
      581.28
    ],
    "text": "alia in respect of all matters for which regulations are required, for carrying out the provisions",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      590.63,
      537.81,
      601.92
    ],
    "text": "of the IDA Act or giving effect to its principles and this power cannot be re\u2010delegated,",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      611.33,
      293.49,
      622.62
    ],
    "text": "circumvented or abdicated in any manner.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      629.65,
      537.81,
      643.32
    ],
    "text": "The Petitioners contend that a predecessor of the 1st Respondent issued Circular No. 02/2011",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.507699966430664,
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      650.35,
      537.81,
      663.96
    ],
    "text": "marked P7 in contravention of the power vested exclusively in the 2nd Respondent Minister and",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.507699966430664,
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      673.31,
      342.81,
      684.6
    ],
    "text": "as such P7 is ultra vires and in excess of his authority.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      735.05,
      537.59,
      757.98
    ],
    "text": "Page 4 of 6",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri-Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.330300331115723
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      53.09,
      312.81,
      64.38
    ],
    "text": "The Petitioners are seeking the following relief:",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      110.64,
      71.98,
      537.8,
      85.02
    ],
    "text": "(a) A writ of certiorari quashing the regulations bearing No. 02/2011 dated 01/03/2011",
    "fonts": [
      "ArialMT",
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      127.61,
      94.37,
      182.31,
      105.66
    ],
    "text": "marked P7;",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      110.63,
      112.75,
      537.81,
      126.42
    ],
    "text": "(b) A writ of mandamus directing the 2nd Respondent to proceed to take steps forthwith",
    "fonts": [
      "ArialMT",
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.507699966430664,
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      127.62,
      135.77,
      537.81,
      147.06
    ],
    "text": "under section 39 of the Industrial Disputes Act No. 43 of 1950 (as amended) and carry",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      127.62,
      156.41,
      537.81,
      167.7
    ],
    "text": "out his statutory duty and obligation to formulate regulations to give meaningful effect",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      127.62,
      177.11,
      537.81,
      188.4
    ],
    "text": "to the provisions of Section 32A of the Industrial Disputes Act (Amendment) No. 56 of",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      127.62,
      197.75,
      155.91,
      209.04
    ],
    "text": "1999.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      218.45,
      537.81,
      229.74
    ],
    "text": "Upon a perusal of Section 32A of the IDA Act (As amended by Act No. 56 of 1999) there can be",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      239.15,
      537.8,
      250.44
    ],
    "text": "no doubt that the Commissioner of Labour or an officer authorized by him in that behalf is",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.71,
      259.79,
      537.81,
      271.08
    ],
    "text": "empowered to conduct a poll at any work place in order to ascertain whether at least forty per",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      280.43,
      537.81,
      291.72
    ],
    "text": "centum of the workmen on whose behalf the trade union seeks to bargain with the employer,",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      301.19,
      254.43,
      312.48
    ],
    "text": "are members of such trade union.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      321.83,
      537.81,
      333.12
    ],
    "text": "The scope and ambit of this power must be understood in the context of rules of statutory",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      342.47,
      166.41,
      353.76
    ],
    "text": "interpretation.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      363.17,
      537.81,
      374.46
    ],
    "text": "In Liyanage and Others v. Gampaha Urban Council and Others [(1991) 1 Sri.L.R. 1] it was held",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      383.81,
      537.82,
      395.1
    ],
    "text": "that in construing instruments that confer power what is not permitted should be taken as",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      404.51,
      537.81,
      415.8
    ],
    "text": "forbidden. This strict doctrine of ultra vires ought to be reasonably and not unreasonably",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      425.21,
      537.81,
      436.5
    ],
    "text": "understood and applied. Whatever may fairly be regarded as incidental to or consequential",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      445.85,
      537.81,
      457.14
    ],
    "text": "upon those things which the Legislature has authorised ought not (unless expressly prohibited)",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      466.49,
      537.82,
      477.78
    ],
    "text": "to be held by judicial construction, to be ultra vires. Acts of statutory authorities that go beyond",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      487.19,
      537.81,
      498.48
    ],
    "text": "the strict letter of this enabling provision can reasonably be considered as being incidental to or",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      507.89,
      537.82,
      519.18
    ],
    "text": "consequential upon that which is permitted, been done with a view to promoting the general",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      528.53,
      537.81,
      539.82
    ],
    "text": "legislative purpose in the conferment of power to such authorities. This is in keeping with the",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      549.23,
      537.81,
      560.52
    ],
    "text": "purposive approach to statutory interpretation. Anything that is contrary to or inconsistent with",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      569.87,
      537.82,
      581.16
    ],
    "text": "such general legislative purpose should not be held as valid by courts in an exercise of statutory",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      590.51,
      166.41,
      601.8
    ],
    "text": "interpretation.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      611.27,
      537.81,
      622.56
    ],
    "text": "The learned counsel for the Petitioners submitted that the power to make regulations is with",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      631.91,
      537.82,
      643.2
    ],
    "text": "the Minister which has been encroached upon in this instance by the Commissioner of Labour.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      652.55,
      537.81,
      663.84
    ],
    "text": "In other words, he sought to establish that P7 contains regulations which only the Minister is",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      673.25,
      228.27,
      684.54
    ],
    "text": "empowered to promulgate.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      693.95,
      537.82,
      705.24
    ],
    "text": "Upon a careful consideration of P7 it is evident that the Commissioner of Labour did not mean",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      714.59,
      537.82,
      725.88
    ],
    "text": "to lay down any regulations therein. The word \u201cregulation\u201d is not found in P7. It is termed",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      735.05,
      537.59,
      757.98
    ],
    "text": "Page 5 of 6",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri-Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.330300331115723
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      53.09,
      537.81,
      64.38
    ],
    "text": "merely as a \u201ccircular\u201d. Then again, the use of the term \u201ccircular\u201d is not decisive. There is a great",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      73.73,
      537.81,
      85.02
    ],
    "text": "variation in nomenclature, and it is extremely difficult to say what, if any, substantial difference",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      94.37,
      537.81,
      105.66
    ],
    "text": "there is between an order, a special order, a rule and a regulation [Law and Orders, Carleton",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      115.13,
      174.21,
      126.42
    ],
    "text": "Kemp Allen, 45].",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      133.39,
      388.23,
      147.06
    ],
    "text": "Wade and Forsyth, Administrative Law, 8th Ed., page 851 states:",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.507699966430664,
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      127.62,
      156.41,
      537.81,
      167.7
    ],
    "text": "\u201cDepartmental circulars are a common form of administrative document by which",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      127.62,
      177.11,
      537.81,
      188.4
    ],
    "text": "instructions are disseminated, e.g. from a department in Whitehall to its local offices or",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      127.62,
      197.75,
      537.81,
      209.04
    ],
    "text": "to local authorities over which it exercises control. Many such circulars are identified by",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      127.62,
      218.45,
      537.82,
      229.74
    ],
    "text": "serial numbers and published, and many of them contain general statements of",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      127.62,
      239.15,
      537.81,
      250.44
    ],
    "text": "policy\u2026They are therefore of great importance to the public, giving much guidance",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      127.62,
      259.79,
      537.81,
      271.08
    ],
    "text": "about governmental organisation and the exercise of discretionary powers. In",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      127.62,
      280.43,
      495.62,
      291.72
    ],
    "text": "themselves they have no legal effect whatever, having no statutory authority\u201d",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      301.19,
      537.8,
      312.48
    ],
    "text": "Our Courts have adopted a similar approach when it came to deciding whether a \u201ccircular\u201d is a",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      321.83,
      537.81,
      333.12
    ],
    "text": "\u201cregulation\u201d having statutory authority. In Piyasiri v. People\u2019s Bank [(1989) 2 Sri.L.R. 47] a staff",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      342.47,
      537.8,
      353.76
    ],
    "text": "circular was considered to be only a circular and not a regulation having statutory force. The",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      363.17,
      537.81,
      374.46
    ],
    "text": "Supreme Court in Weligama Multi\u2010Purpose Co\u2010operative Society Ltd., v. Chandradasa Daluwatta",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      383.81,
      537.82,
      395.1
    ],
    "text": "[(1984) 1 Sri.L.R. 195] held a circular not to be a regulation and that it did not have the status or",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      404.51,
      537.81,
      415.8
    ],
    "text": "attribute of a regulation. In Mallika and Others v. Ruhunu Development Bank [(2008) 2 Sri.L.R.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      425.21,
      537.82,
      436.5
    ],
    "text": "177] this Court held the impugned circular to be a communication between the administration",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      445.85,
      210.15,
      457.14
    ],
    "text": "of the bank and its staff.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      466.49,
      537.81,
      477.78
    ],
    "text": "The Circular No. 02/2011 (P7) is an internal circular addressed to several designated officers of",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      487.19,
      537.82,
      498.48
    ],
    "text": "the Department of Labour and sets out the procedure that should be followed in conducting a",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.73,
      507.89,
      537.81,
      519.18
    ],
    "text": "poll at any work place in order to ascertain whether at least forty per centum of the workmen",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      528.53,
      537.81,
      539.82
    ],
    "text": "on whose behalf the trade union seeks to bargain with the employer, are members of such",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      549.23,
      152.67,
      560.52
    ],
    "text": "trade union.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      569.87,
      537.81,
      581.16
    ],
    "text": "Where the Commissioner of Labour has been empowered to conduct a poll, in the absence of",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      590.51,
      537.81,
      601.8
    ],
    "text": "specific statutory provisions governing the conduct of such poll, Commissioner of Labour has",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      611.27,
      537.81,
      622.56
    ],
    "text": "the power to decide the procedure to be followed in the conduct of such poll. Such an",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      631.91,
      537.81,
      643.2
    ],
    "text": "interpretation in my view can reasonably be considered as being incidental to or consequential",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      652.55,
      537.8,
      663.84
    ],
    "text": "upon that which is permitted, being done with a view to promoting the general legislative",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      673.25,
      510.87,
      684.54
    ],
    "text": "purpose in the conferment of power on the Commissioner of Labour to conduct such poll.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      693.95,
      537.82,
      705.24
    ],
    "text": "That is exactly what the Commissioner of Labour has done by P7. It provides for the procedure",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      714.59,
      537.81,
      725.88
    ],
    "text": "to be followed in conducting the poll he has been authorised to do. It lays down what may be",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      735.05,
      537.59,
      757.98
    ],
    "text": "Page 6 of 6",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri-Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.330300331115723
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      53.09,
      537.81,
      64.38
    ],
    "text": "termed as guidelines in the conduct of the poll. Such guidelines assist in establishing",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      73.73,
      486.99,
      85.02
    ],
    "text": "transparency and consistency in the conduct of such poll and prevents arbitrariness.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      92.05,
      537.81,
      105.66
    ],
    "text": "It does not in any way contravene any power vested exclusively in the 2nd Respondent Minister",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.507699966430664,
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      115.13,
      290.19,
      126.42
    ],
    "text": "in particular his regulation making power.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      133.39,
      537.81,
      147.06
    ],
    "text": "Section 39(1) of the IDA Act specifies the areas in which the 2nd Respondent Minister may make",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.507699966430664,
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      156.41,
      537.81,
      167.7
    ],
    "text": "regulations. None of them deal with the procedure to be followed in the conduct of such poll.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      177.11,
      537.82,
      188.4
    ],
    "text": "Therefore, I hold that P7 is not ultra vires the power of the Commissioner General of Labour.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      93.73,
      197.75,
      315.76,
      209.04
    ],
    "text": "The writ of mandamus also fails for that reason.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      93.73,
      218.45,
      395.43,
      229.74
    ],
    "text": "For the aforesaid reasons, I dismiss the application without costs.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      301.19,
      430.41,
      312.48
    ],
    "text": "Judge of the Court of Appeal",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      349.97,
      224.19,
      361.26
    ],
    "text": "N. Bandula Karunarathna J.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri-Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      406.37,
      299.79,
      417.66
    ],
    "text": "I agree.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 5,
    "bbox": [
      93.72,
      462.77,
      430.41,
      474.06
    ],
    "text": "Judge of the Court of Appeal",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.289799690246582
    ]
  }
]